# RA-9: `//` is a comment in style blocks, so an unquoted URL swallows the
# rest of the line, including the rule's `}`. The `}` on the last line then
# closes the `.a` rule, leaving the style block open (a parser error).
StyleKw "style"
LBrace "{"
Newline "\n"
Dot "."
Ident "a"
LBrace "{"
Ident "background"
Colon ":"
Ident "url"
LParen "("
Ident "https"
Colon ":"
LineComment "//x.com/a.png); }"
Newline "\n"
RBrace "}"
Newline "\n"
